      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(apply): reconcile labels after re-review commands",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nClawSweeper could publish a complete fresh-head PR review with `proof: sufficient` and a diamond rating while leaving older `needs proof` and silver labels on the PR. A command-only `@clawsweeper re-review` comment was filtered from review context as intended, but GitHub's duplicate body-less `commented` timeline event still made the label freshness gate treat it as new substantive human activity.\n\nObserved on https://github.com/steipete/CodexBar/pull/1869#issuecomment-4880229473.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nIssue comments are already checked with their bodies. For fresh-review label reconciliation only, ignore duplicate timeline `commented` events so command-only re-review comments do not block the labels produced by the review they requested.\n\nThe relaxation is deliberately scoped to label sync. Close promotion and other mutation safety paths still treat a command-only re-review request as human activity.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAfter a successful re-review, ClawSweeper now removes stale proof/rating/status labels and applies the labels matching the current durable review. Explicit re-review requests continue to block stale-PR close promotion.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Regression: `node --test --test-name-pattern='command-only re-review|humans act after' test/apply-label-sync.test.ts`\n- Close-safety regression: `node --test --test-name-pattern='command-only re-review request' test/apply-pr-promotion.test.ts`\n- Full repository gate: `pnpm run check`\n- Autoreview: clean after one accepted safety finding was fixed by scoping timeline deduplication to label reconciliation.\n",
        "branch": "codex/fix-rereview-label-reconciliation",
